  "body": "## Change and scope\n\nAt base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`, the historical inplace-side prefix checker (`scripts/experiments/inplace_side.py:verify_prefix`) rejects a specified n-role Gauss\u2013Jordan side family using three pinned witnesses (`h = 42, 46, 50`). Each elimination column previously rebuilt `sorted(unused)` to locate the least unused row with the pivot bit set.\n\nThis PR replaces that search with a least-unused flag scan and column masks. The lexicographic pivot rule, XOR updates, switch witnesses, deficit arithmetic and every receipt field are unchanged. Only the source pin for `scripts/experiments/inplace_side.py` changes inside `certificates/inplace-side.json`.\n\n**Tooling improvement; no new kappa.** The selected frontier, `upstream/`, and the mathematical rejection in `docs/research/inplace-side.md` are not reopened.\n\n## Result\n\nOn Linux / CPython 3.12.3, five alternating fresh-process pairs of the three pinned witnesses gave median **17.061 s \u2192 5.466 s (3.12\u00d7)**. Timing is host-descriptive and is not a correctness gate. Receipts match the byte-identical baseline checker fieldwise; a greatest-unused mutant is rejected on all three witnesses.\n\nPackage: `research/inplace-side-performance/`.\n\n## Validation\n\nPython **3.12**, standard library only:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/inplace-side-performance/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -O -B research/inplace-side-performance/verify.py\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/inplace-side-performance\npython3.12 -I -B research/inplace-side-performance/benchmark.py --rounds 5\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n```text\nPASS_INPLACE_SIDE_PREFIX_FAST witnesses=3 h=[42, 46, 50] paths=[151, 415, 767] ... no_new_kappa\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/inplace-side-performance outcome=completed\nPASS_IDENTICAL_INPLACE_PREFIX_RECEIPTS\n```\n\nDefault verify is read-only. Use `--write-certificate` only after editing the production source. Full `make verify`, selected cold replay, Lean, and multiplication-theorem obligations were not rerun for this isolated historical-checker change.\n\n## Overlap and credit\n\nClosest priors (different objects): [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#756](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/756) packed balanced-Fano replay; [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1584](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1584) finite-bit block-core frame interning; [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1076](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1076) / [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1075](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1075) quadratic tooling. No competing open PR on this inplace-side object at refresh.\n\nDouglas R. Colkitt authored the inplace-side rejection, witnesses and original checker. Prepared by Wentao Li ([VictorLiwentao](https://github.com/VictorLiwentao), [@Is__Victor](https://x.com/Is__Victor)) with substantial AI assistance, under Apache-2.0.",
